{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Phase 2: Predictive Maintenance Exploratory Data Analysis (AI4I 2020)\n",
    "## Project: Adaptive Learning for Cloud Security and Predictive Maintenance\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective:\n",
    "Perform statistical and visual EDA on the **AI4I 2020 Predictive Maintenance Dataset** to analyze machine failure class balance, sensor distributions, correlations, and feature separation between normal vs. failing machines. All plots are automatically saved to `results/maintenance/eda/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Styling settings\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"muted\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 11, 'figure.autolayout': True})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Paths\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))) if '__file__' in locals() else os.path.abspath('..')\n",
    "DATA_PATH = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, 'data', 'maintenance', 'ai4i2020.csv')\n",
    "SAVE_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, 'results', 'maintenance', 'eda')\n",
    "os.makedirs(SAVE_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load AI4I 2020 dataset\n",
    "df_maint = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"AI4I 2020 Loaded successfully! Shape: {df_maint.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 1. Machine Failure Distribution (Class Balance)\n",
    "Visualizing class proportions for the primary binary target `Machine failure` (0 = Normal, 1 = Failure)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
    "counts = df_maint['Machine failure'].value_counts()\n",
    "pcts = df_maint['Machine failure'].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "bars = ax.bar(['No Failure (0)', 'Machine Failure (1)'], counts, color=['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c'], width=0.5)\n",
    "for bar, pct in zip(bars, pcts):\n",
    "    height = bar.get_height()\n",
    "    ax.annotate(f'{height:,} ({pct:.1f}%)',\n",
    "                xy=(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width() / 2, height),\n",
    "                xytext=(0, 3), textcoords=\"offset points\",\n",
    "                ha='center', va='bottom', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"AI4I 2020: Machine Failure Class Balance\", fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "save_path = os.path.join(SAVE_DIR, 'machine_failure_distribution.png')\n",
    "plt.savefig(save_path, dpi=300)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(f\"Saved: {save_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plot Interpretation (Machine Failure Distribution):\n",
    "The target distribution displays **severe class imbalance**. Normal machine operation accounts for **92.3%** (1,846 samples) of the dataset, while machine failure accounts for only **7.7%** (154 samples). This reflects realistic industrial operating conditions where equipment failure is a rare event. Preprocessing and modeling in Part 3/6 must incorporate imbalance handling (e.g., SMOTE, class weights, or focal loss) to avoid high accuracy scores that mask poor failure detection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 2. Sensor Value Distributions\n",
    "Individual histogram plots for Air Temperature, Process Temperature, Rotational Speed, Torque, and Tool Wear."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sensors = [\n",
    "    ('Air temperature [K]', 'air_temperature_distribution.png', '#e67e22'),\n",
    "    ('Process temperature [K]', 'process_temperature_distribution.png', '#e74c3c'),\n",
    "    ('Rotational speed [rpm]', 'rotational_speed_distribution.png', '#3498db'),\n",
    "    ('Torque [Nm]', 'torque_distribution.png', '#9b59b6'),\n",
    "    ('Tool wear [min]', 'tool_wear_distribution.png', '#1abc9c')\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "for col, filename, color in sensors:\n",
    "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4.5))\n",
    "    sns.histplot(df_maint[col], kde=True, ax=ax, color=color, bins=30)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"AI4I 2020: {col} Distribution\", fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(col)\n",
    "    save_path = os.path.join(SAVE_DIR, filename)\n",
    "    plt.savefig(save_path, dpi=300)\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    print(f\"Saved: {save_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plot Interpretations (Sensor Distributions):\n",
    "1. **Air & Process Temperatures**: Both display near-normal, Gaussian distributions centered around 298 K (Air) and 309 K (Process).\n",
    "2. **Rotational Speed**: Displays a right-skewed distribution centered around 1,500 rpm with a long tail extending past 2,500 rpm.\n",
    "3. **Torque**: Displays a symmetrical, bell-shaped distribution centered around 40 Nm.\n",
    "4. **Tool Wear**: Displays a uniform distribution spanning 0 to 240 minutes, reflecting continuous tool usage over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 3. Correlation Heatmap\n",
    "Pairwise correlation matrix across continuous operational settings, sensors, and machine failure targets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "num_cols_maint = [\n",
    "    'Air temperature [K]', 'Process temperature [K]', 'Rotational speed [rpm]',\n",
    "    'Torque [Nm]', 'Tool wear [min]', 'Machine failure'\n",
    "]\n",
    "corr_maint = df_maint[num_cols_maint].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 7))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr_maint, annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", cmap=\"coolwarm\", center=0, ax=ax, cbar_kws={'label': 'Pearson Correlation'})\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"AI4I 2020: Maintenance Feature Correlation Heatmap\", fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "save_path = os.path.join(SAVE_DIR, 'maintenance_correlation_heatmap.png')\n",
    "plt.savefig(save_path, dpi=300)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(f\"Saved: {save_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plot Interpretation (Correlation Heatmap):\n",
    "The correlation matrix demonstrates a **strong positive correlation ($r = 0.88$)** between `Air temperature [K]` and `Process temperature [K]`. Additionally, there is a **strong inverse correlation ($r = -0.87$)** between `Rotational speed [rpm]` and `Torque [Nm]`, matching physical power laws ($P = \tau \cdot \omega$). `Torque [Nm]` and `Tool wear [min]` show the highest direct positive linear correlation with `Machine failure`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 4. Key Sensor Values Split by Machine Failure (Boxplots)\n",
    "Comparing sensor distributions between normal operation (`Machine failure = 0`) and failed machines (`Machine failure = 1`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sensor_names = ['Air temperature [K]', 'Process temperature [K]', 'Rotational speed [rpm]', 'Torque [Nm]', 'Tool wear [min]']\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(15, 9))\n",
    "axes = axes.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "for idx, col in enumerate(sensor_names):\n",
    "    sns.boxplot(data=df_maint, x='Machine failure', y=col, ax=axes[idx], palette=['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c'])\n",
    "    axes[idx].set_title(f\"{col} vs. Failure\", fontsize=11, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "    axes[idx].set_xticklabels(['Normal (0)', 'Failure (1)'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove empty subplot\n",
    "fig.delaxes(axes[5])\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"AI4I 2020: Sensor Distributions Split by Machine Failure\", fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "save_path = os.path.join(SAVE_DIR, 'sensor_boxplots_by_failure.png')\n",
    "plt.savefig(save_path, dpi=300)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(f\"Saved: {save_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Plot Interpretation (Boxplots Split by Failure):\n",
    "The boxplots show clear physical separation between normal operating states and machine failure states:\n",
    "1. **Torque [Nm]**: Failed machines exhibit significantly higher median torque levels ($> 55 \\text{ Nm}$) and extreme lower/upper torque outliers compared to normal operation.\n",
    "2. **Tool Wear [min]**: Machines that fail show markedly higher cumulative tool wear ($> 180 \\text{ minutes}$).\n",
    "3. **Rotational Speed [rpm]**: Failed machines show higher concentrations of extreme low-speed and high-speed outliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 5. Statistical Summary Table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "maint_stats = df_maint[sensor_names].describe().T\n",
    "display(maint_stats)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 6. Key Observations Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "> ### 📌 Summary of Observations (AI4I 2020):\n",
    "> 1. **Severe Class Imbalance**: Machine failure occurs in only **7.7%** of samples (154 failures vs 1,846 normal operations). Imbalance techniques (SMOTE, class weighting) are essential for Part 3/6.\n",
    "> 2. **Physical Inverse Correlation**: `Rotational speed [rpm]` and `Torque [Nm]` have a strong inverse correlation ($r = -0.87$). High torque / low speed conditions correlate heavily with Power and Overstrain failures.\n",
    "> 3. **Top Failure Predictors**: `Torque [Nm]` and `Tool wear [min]` show the clearest distribution separation between normal and failed states.\n",
    "> 4. **Temperature Collinearity**: `Air temperature [K]` and `Process temperature [K]` are highly collinear ($r = 0.88$). A temperature difference feature ($\Delta T = T_{\\text{proc}} - T_{\\text{air}}$) will be a powerful engineered feature in Part 3."
   ]
  }
 ],
